 "notes": "Label column = outside dimensions (side x side) in mm, written with a lower-case letter x as printed; the other column labels = wall thickness in mm; cell values = theoretical mass in kg/m (decimal point as printed). Empty cells are empty in the source; no footnotes, no merged cells. 21 rows. Two values are printed with only two decimals: '0.82' (19x19 / 1.5) and '1.45' (20x20 / 3.0) - kept as printed. Source image is a JPEG. Observation for the verification step (no value was changed): all 204 printed values equal round(0.00785*(4*a*t - c*t*t), 3) with c = 4 + (4-pi)*0.25 = 4.2146 for wall thicknesses 0.8-2.5 and c = 4 + (4-pi)*2.5 = 6.146 for the 3.0 column (a = side, t = wall), i.e. the source apparently assumes almost sharp corners up to 2.5 mm and a much larger corner radius for 3.0 mm. Consequently the step from column 2.5 to column 3.0 is small (e.g. 18x18: 1.206 -> 1.261), and all values are heavier than a formula with corner radii ro=2T / ri=T (c = 6.575) would give."
